---
description: KiwiEngine C++ formatting and naming preferences
alwaysApply: true
---

# Keep statements and signatures on one line

Do not wrap a single call, assignment, function declaration or definition signature across multiple lines, no matter how long it gets.

```cpp
// BAD
ViewUB = TUniformBufferRef<ViewUniformBuffer>::CreateEmptyUniformBufferImmediate(
    device, EUniformBufferUsage::SingleFrame, "ViewUniformBuffer");

void Render(RHICommandContext* ctx, RHITextureView* sceneRTV,
    const Viewport& viewport, const ScissorRect& scissor);

// GOOD
ViewUB = TUniformBufferRef<ViewUniformBuffer>::CreateEmptyUniformBufferImmediate(device, EUniformBufferUsage::SingleFrame, "ViewUniformBuffer");

void Render(RHICommandContext* ctx, RHITextureView* sceneRTV, const Viewport& viewport, const ScissorRect& scissor);
```

Constructor initializer lists, lambda bodies and brace blocks still go on their own lines as usual.

# Naming

- Everything is PascalCase with no prefix: types, functions, member variables, public struct fields, local variables and parameters. No `m_`, and no Unreal `F`/`U` type prefixes.
- Bool members may use a `b` prefix (`bShouldClose`, `bIsDragging`).
- A parameter that would collide with a member or type gets an `In` prefix (`SceneRenderer(KiwiEngineApp& InApp) : App(InApp)`, `ComputeViewVisibility(const Scene& InScene)`). A local that would collide gets a more specific name (`Frustum ViewFrustum;`, `Hit PrimaryHit;`).
- When a member has the same name as its type (`Scene Scene;`, `std::unique_ptr<SceneRenderer> SceneRenderer;`), the bare name means the member inside that class. Write the type as `Kiwi::Scene` there.
- A member must not share a name with a method of the same class, the class itself, or a nested type. Pick another name (`bShouldClose` next to `ShouldClose()`, `ViewType` next to `enum class Type`).
- Shader source embedded in C++ strings keeps shader naming; do not rename inside it.

```cpp
// BAD
SceneRenderer* m_SceneRenderer;
MeshBatch batch;
void Render(RHICommandContext* ctx, const Viewport& vp);

// GOOD
std::unique_ptr<SceneRenderer> SceneRenderer;
MeshBatch Batch;
void Render(RHICommandContext* Ctx, const Viewport& Vp);
```

Older files outside the renderer (editor, RHI backends, resource setup) still use camelCase locals and parameters. Write new code in PascalCase; convert an old file only when asked.
